.SH NAME
SIZE860 - Displays section sizes of iPSC\*R/860\fR\fR\fR\fR\& object files. 
.\" End Summary
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
\&\fBsize860\fR\fR\& [ \fR\fIoptions\fI\fR\& ] \fR\fIfilenames\fI\fR\
\& 
.SH ARGUMENTS 
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fR\fIfilename\fI\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' The name of the iPSC/860\& object file. 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.LP
You may specify the following \fR\fIoptions\fI\fR\& in any order:
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-o\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Display sizes in octal.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-x\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Display sizes in hexadecimal.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-d\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Display sizes in decimal (default).
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-n\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Display the sizes of non-loading sections, as well.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-f\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Full output.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-V\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Display the tool banner (tool name, version, etc.).
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
Use \fBsize860\fR\fR\& to display the section sizes of the named files. 
.LP
Note that the total size of an executable object may be greater than or less than the total of the sizes \
of all the compiled objects that make up the executable. This is because the true size of the BSS \
section is not known until after a set of objects is loaded, and because padding is done by \fB\
ld860\fR\fR\& on other sections. 
.SH SEE ALSO
.LP
